{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1191189-discussing-on-allegiances","id":1191189,"title":"Discussing on Allegiances","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-02T18:30:11-08:00","id":1191189,"title":"Discussing on Allegiances","content":"So obviously some of the Allegiances in the Trinity Core have thematic overlap, which is cool, but I'm wondering about people's takes on the distinctions.<br /> <br /> What source material would you site for stories built around the different Allegiances (ala &quot;Agents of SHIELD&quot; for 9, and &quot;Person of Interest&quot; for Pharaoh's Lightkeepers)?<br /> <br /> To give more specific example questions...<br /> <br /> What type of stories is Alert Status 1 meant to cover that 9 does not? 9 primarily does intelligence work, and is similarly not specific-government aligned.<br /> <br /> What type of work does the Aeon Society itself, than neither of its spin-offs, nor the Cartography Initiative, do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-02-2018, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T01:06:57-08:00","id":1191282,"title":"","content":"I'd have to sit and think a bit for broader stuff, but to tackle one of your specific examples...<br /> <br /> Alert Status 1, at least to the best of my understanding, is more espionage-focused. Think True Lies, or Mission Impossible. Disguises, cover identities, surveillance equipment, the comic relief tech guy. Finding the villain's volcano lair.<br /> <br /> 9 is a little more focused on the technology -- the episode of Agents of SHIELD where they're dealing with 'Centipede,' or much of the first season of Fringe. Figuring out just how the bad guy's sonic disintegrator works and how the technology was developed and using that to trace it back to the source.<br /> <br /> The difference between them would be that when the bad guy's in their volcano lair with the sonic disintegrator, Alert Status 1 will go up the unscalable side of the volcano, knock out a guard and infiltrate the base while another member of the team has managed to take the place of one of the villain's lieutenants. 9 might go in a little more guns blazing, confident in themselves because they developed a quantum feedback shield that can counter the disintegrator.<br /> <br /> And when the volcano lair is about to explode for some reason, the Alert Status 1 agent will have a technician (and/or a defected flunkie of the villain) on the comms telling them what wires to cut until they get it at the last minute. The team of operatives from 9, however, will bring one of the team's science experts over to it and they'll come up with some means of using the villain's own tech to neutralize the explosives.<br /> <br /> At least, that's just my personal read, entirely brainstorming stuff up on the fly here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T14:00:01-08:00","id":1191445,"title":"","content":"To me, that just sounds like tactical differences that you'd find within the same Allegiance (i.e. varied PC options within the same group). Surely 9 maintain covert operatives in order to be an intelligence agency.in addition to mirror-shaded response teams?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T15:43:38-08:00","id":1191465,"title":"","content":"9 almost certainly has some specialized covert operatives just as Alert Status 1 has some scientists. But the fact that they approach problems in different ways is as much a reflection of internal culture than simply tactical differences. After all, multiple branches of the US military have access to aircraft and explosives, and I dare you to tell any of the soldiers in those branches that it's only tactical differences that separate them.<br /> <br /> Also, I'll admit I was trying too hard to be clever by describing different solutions to the same problem, but I'm pretty sure they also focus on different threats most of the time. 9 wouldn't be likely to get dragged into an intricate, relatively low-tech conspiracy meant to overthrow one or more world governments, and if someone is robbing banks with a machine that gets them through vault walls, Alert Status 1 wouldn't even crack the top 3 in organizations the authorities might try to contact.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm pretty sure some overlap is intentional to allow for mixed groups, crossover games, and the like. (&quot;Agent Tasker, see if we can get Coulson to loan us Fitzsimmons for this one, he owes us a favor.&quot;) Also, it helps that Allegiances can be a little broad to allow for a wider variety of stories within each, so every Alert Status 1 story isn't just a different Mission Impossible movie, for instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T21:15:56-08:00","id":1191526,"title":"","content":"Adventures with operatives from 9 or from Alert Status 9 will be very similar as the two organizations... the main difference is general scope.<br /> <br /> 9 deals with threats to the USA... if it has nothing to do with any United States interest, then it likely doesn't fall in 9's jurisdiction. If an operative of 9 is on vacation in another part of the world and happens on a local threat, chances are that he will not do anything unless he is personally involved or it threatens a US interest in the area. &quot;The problems of others are not our problems,&quot; is likely something one of their superiors would say should the operative report the situation.<br /> <br /> Alert Status 1 however is international in scope... and while they have operatives from the USA, they will deal with threats that may not actually have much impact on the United States. If a US born operative in the States is in Italy and happens across a plot that could destabilize the area, he will likely alter other members of AS1 and together deal with the situation, even if there is little to no chance of this threat being a threat to US interests.<br /> <br /> While both use similar methods and tactics, the difference is the scope of the threats they will face. 9 mostly deals with direct threats to the USA... while AS1 will deal with threats of an international level regardless of who is directly threatened.<br /> <br /> So why choose one over the other? Again, scope. If the game will only be within in the borders of the United States, then chances are than agents of 9 see the most action, while a more international level of play is likely to see AS1 operatives getting more spotlight. Yes, there is a chance for overlap with both, but an agent of 9 is less likely to be deployed internationally when the threat doesn't affect or involve the USA; while AS1 operatives are unlikely to be needed to deal with a local threat within the USA unless it has the likelihood of becoming an international threat. By the same token, if there is an international level threat that could threaten US interests, chances are that an agent of 9 and an AS1 operative could find themselves working together on the same case (though whether act cross purposes or not is left to the ST).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T22:03:22-08:00","id":1191539,"title":"","content":"Alert Status 1:<br /> <br /> - Primarily intelligence/counter-intelligence<br /> - Government-funded<br /> - International<br /> - They deal with mundane threats: coups, kidnappings, assassinations, bioweapon threats, etc.<br /> - If you want to play your standard superspy game, this is the group. Man from UNCLE, James Bond, Bourne Identity. Less serious: Get Smart, Archer<br /> <br /> 9:<br /> <br /> - Less CIA and more FBI. Goal is more investigation than espionage.<br /> - Privately-run organization<br /> - While they're branching out internationally -- see their association with the UN Security Council -- their focus is still largely American<br /> - They deal with extraordinary threats (usually Inspired individuals or Inspired tech), not mundane ones<br /> - If you want to play X-Files, Agents of SHIELD, this is the group.<br /> <br /> There's some overlap, sure, and agents and operatives from both organizations can certainly team up where their needs overlap. And maybe they'll argue about who has jurisdiction if both of them show up on a case. An AS1 agent investigating the kidnapping of a dignitary and a 9 agent investigating a recently-abandoned local outpost of the notorious Order of Murder might need to work together when it turns out that the dignitary was kidnapped by his own clone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T22:31:25-08:00","id":1191543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1191189-discussing-on-allegiances?p=1191526#post1191526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">9 deals with threats to the USA... if it has nothing to do with any United States interest, then it likely doesn't fall in 9's jurisdiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s... explicitly not true in the book text. 9 is a multinational private contractor that works with many governments, the UN, and other entities. NOER is the US government\u2019s closest equivelent we have in present day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T01:03:02-08:00","id":1191569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1191189-discussing-on-allegiances?p=1191539#post1191539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alert Status 1:<br /> <br /> - Primarily intelligence/counter-intelligence<br /> - Government-funded<br /> - International<br /> - They deal with mundane threats: coups, kidnappings, assassinations, bioweapon threats, etc.<br /> - If you want to play your standard superspy game, this is the group. Man from UNCLE, James Bond, Bourne Identity. Less serious: Get Smart, Archer</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait... what government funds them? I thought they were an autonomous network made up of deactivated assets?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T01:15:36-08:00","id":1191574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1191189-discussing-on-allegiances?p=1191539#post1191539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 9:<br /> <br /> - Less CIA and more FBI. Goal is more investigation than espionage.<br /> - Privately-run organization<br /> - While they're branching out internationally -- see their association with the UN Security Council -- their focus is still largely American<br /> - They deal with extraordinary threats (usually Inspired individuals or Inspired tech), not mundane ones<br /> - If you want to play X-Files, Agents of SHIELD, this is the group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I'm getting the distinction from Alert Status 1, but in that process I'm having a harder time seeing their distinction from NOER, save for the fact that NOER is still officially US government. I had been interpreting them as more the FBI-style response to the paranormal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T09:51:17-08:00","id":1191643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1191189-discussing-on-allegiances?p=1191569#post1191569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait... what government funds them? I thought they were an autonomous network made up of deactivated assets?</div> </div> </div> </div>While they are largely autonomous in operation, &quot;Many founding nations have formalized departments funded by their governments\u2019 defense budgets, while others never developed such a bureaucratic system and remain as small cells connected only by back channel communications.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T11:04:30-08:00","id":1191683,"title":"","content":"Thanks Ian, you are helping a lot!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T11:10:40-08:00","id":1191686,"title":"","content":"From what was said about 9 in the preview, it was created to be an arm of the US Government... so while it may take on International Level threats, those threats will be ones directed at the US (and possibly its allies). If it isn't directed at either the US or its allies (or at least their interests), chances are that Agents will not have official sanction to intervene (unofficially, they may be encouraged or even allowed to use their own discretion, though will be disavowed should such an operation go south).<br /> <br /> To be honest though, many of these organizations are very similar... sort of the difference of flavor between regular Chocolate ice cream and Triple Chocolate Fudge ice cream. Which you prefer will depend on how you wish to run a game. Do you want a game where the players are heavily constricted by the procedures they MUST follow (by-the-book type operations where even a slight variation can get one in trouble even if the results justify the means), one with less emphasis on how things are done (where results are all that really matter) or one where there are few to no rules governing what tactics players are free to try (though obvious abuse of such power will be sanctions, probably harshly).<br /> <br /> Different Organizations will have different levels of rules for its members to follow. Collaborating with a known &quot;enemy&quot; agent from a hostile nation against a greater threat may stop that threat, but could lead to serious reprimands for an agent of 9 regardless of the results of the mission, but could be a commended action by an operative working for Alert Status 1. While the two are very similar in styles of adventures and types of characters one will see... it is the role-playing aspects that really set them apart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T11:48:56-08:00","id":1191699,"title":"","content":"Right now for my own table i\u2019m leaning toward collapsing NOER into 9 (possibly replacing NOER with an antagonist group that are the US\u2019s overly militaristic response to paranormal threats/trying to weaponize said phenomena); giving the Global Cartography Initiative\u2019s whole academic focus to the Aeon Society (on the premise the Aeon Society learns, and Triton and Neptune use that knowledge to actively better the world in their respective manners); and dropping the Pharaoh\u2019s Lightkeepers in favor of giving Archangel a mysterious unknown benefactor that recruits do gooders through cryptic messages around the world, rather than a known aristocrat just bankrolling what\u2019s essentially a paramilitary.<br /> <br /> This is in addition to numerous villain factions I\u2019m working on, like Sovereign - which is the far right counterpart to LRE. Think of the villains from Season 1 of Designated Survivor or Season 2 of Quantico.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}